<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">Satiru uprising</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1906">1906</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Satiru revolt</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Satiru uprising was a Mahdist rising in 1906 at the village of Satiru near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sokoto-caliphate">Sokoto</a>, in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/northern-nigeria-protectorate">Protectorate of Northern Nigeria</a>. The rebels destroyed a British-led company in February, but in March a larger force, supported by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan-of-sokoto">Sultan of Sokoto</a>, crushed them, killing many villagers and razing Satiru. It was the most serious challenge to British rule in the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a>.</p></div>
